  "review": {
    "label": "curated_editorial",
    "look_ahead": "Stephen Robinson's first full season would begin with a substantial squad rebuild, no European football and a League Cup semi-final against Rangers.\n",
    "read": "The 2025-26 season is the strongest argument for reading the record as a trade-off rather than a verdict. The club was in Europe, defended a trophy and still fell into a relegation worry. The reset to Stephen Robinson is the response; the 2026-27 season is the test of whether it changes the pattern.\n",
    "trade_off": "European league-phase football is a reward for the previous season and a cost in the next: travel, squad depth and league points. The season shows both sides, and the managerial change shows the cost of waiting too long to act.\n",
    "what_did_not": "The league fell to ninth and the club was winless away from home in the 2025-26 league season (January to May 2026). The cup defence ended in a 3-0 quarter-final defeat at Dunfermline. The European league phase produced heavy defeats and a 35th-place finish.\n",
    "what_worked": "The club reached a European league phase and defended the Scottish Cup into the quarter-finals. The managerial search ended with a permanent appointment before the end of the season, giving the next campaign a settled start.\n"
  },
